  "title": "Rota's conjecture on disjoint bases",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "mediawiki-wikitext",
    "text": "Let <math>M</math> be a matroid of rank ''n'' whose ground set ''S'' can be partitioned into ''n'' disjoint bases <math>B_1,\\dots,B_n</math>. Is it true that <math>B_1,\\dots,B_n</math> always have ''n'' disjoint transversals that are bases of <math>M</math>?",
